   "subject": "Re: bug in aaply? Why does aaply(data,2,class) returns “data.frame” for all columns?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "This is expected behaviour (due to complicated reasons relating to\r<br>list-arrays).  What you actually want is either colwise or laply.\r<br>\r<br>Hadley\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Sun, May 20, 2012 at 12:08 PM, greg &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">gregor.h...@googlemail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt; Hi, I was playing around with the plyr function and discovered\r<br>&gt; that aaply(data,2,class) returns a vector of length ncol(data) filled\r<br>&gt; with “data.frame”. I would expect that it returns a vector with the class of\r<br>&gt; the variables in the dataframe. As a consequence, testing which columns are\r<br>&gt; numerical also fails. Below is some code to illustrate my point.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Thanks and best!\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; ps: I started the discussion here\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/q/10673771/1318686\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/q/10673771/1318686&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792358517317000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2uXcPPOe65204twqq2Srzd\">http://stackoverflow.com/q/10673771/1318686</a> and someone pointed me to this\r<br>&gt; list noting &quot;It [the help page] says that dataframe input should be accepted\r<br>&gt; [for a*ply functions] and that an array should be the output. So you have\r<br>&gt; discovered either an error in the documentation or a bug in the function&quot;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; data=data.frame(str=rep(&quot;str&quot;,3),num=c(1:3))\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; class(data[,1])\r<br>&gt; # &quot;factor\r<br>&gt; class(data[,2])\r<br>&gt; # &quot;integer&quot;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; aaply(data,2,class)\r<br>&gt; # &quot;data.frame&quot; &quot;data.frame&quot;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; aaply(data,2,is.numeric)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; # FALSE FALSE\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
